        "outcome": "not-feasible",
        "assessment": "UCR offers transferable historical, rhetorical, qualitative and cultural-analysis methods, but no cumulative music-history sequence, music theory, aural study, score-based analysis, critical listening or musicological research. General history, literature and art history cannot supply the missing musical object and disciplinary methods."
      },
      {
        "concept": "Music, society, politics and cultural institutions",
        "generatingRegistryRows": [
          15459,
          15460,
          15462,
          15468,
          15469,
          15473,
          15477
        ],
        "supportingRegistryRows": [
          15486,
          15487,
          15488,
          15491,
          15492
        ],
        "outcome": "not-feasible",
        "assessment": "Sociology, politics, qualitative research, marketing, art institutions and museum studies can analyse societies and cultural organisations. Their documented content does not sustain a music-centred curriculum in musical scenes, institutions, industries, programming, criticism and political meaning; extending them to 23 non-PPD courses would change the organising field to general sociology, business or cultural studies."
      },
      {
        "concept": "Music, screen media and digital culture",
        "generatingRegistryRows": [
          15464,
          15465,
          15466,
          15467,
          15470,
          15478
        ],
        "supportingRegistryRows": [
          15485,
          15493,
          15494,
          15496,
          15497,
          15498,
          15499
        ],
        "outcome": "not-feasible",
        "assessment": "Film and media courses provide real study of audiovisual form, media technologies, podcasts, documentary and digital platforms. Music or sound appears only as one element or occasional medium. UCR lacks sustained screen-music analysis, recording and production history, interactive/game music, music software, popular-music criticism and musicological progression, so the complete programme would be Media Studies rather than a defensible related Musicology response."
      }
